// C emitter (stage 3). Walks the AST and prints C, mirroring idc.py:
// id functions become `id_NAME`, locals are hoisted to function scope (id is
// function-scoped), a runtime prelude and forward declarations come first, then
// a C main() wrapper. The output is byte-identical to idc.py for the supported
// subset (scalar int/void programs).

emit_program(string triple) {
  emit_head();
  emit_asm_then_main(triple);
  emit_main_wrapper();
} return void;
given nz_prog_fixture ("x86_64-linux"):() then calls emit_main_wrapper:()
given nz_prog_nomain_fixture ("x86_64-linux"):() then calls def_all:()

// runtime prelude, a blank line, then the declarations section, matching
// idc.py's layout exactly
emit_head() {
  emit_runtime();
  emit_line("");
  emit_decls();
} return void;
given nz_prog_fixture ():() then calls emit_decls:()
given nz_prog_nomain_fixture ():() then calls emit_eprint_def:()

// eprint's helper when the program calls it (decl/eprint.id), then the forward
// declarations, then the exported-variable globals (if any) -- idc.py's order
emit_decls() {
  emit_eprint_def();
  emit_fwds();
  emit_exports();
} return void;
given nz_prog_fixture ():() then prints:("/* forward declarations */\nint id_main(int argc);\nvoid id_run(void);\n\n")
given nz_prog_nomain_fixture ():() then prints:("/* forward declarations */\nvoid id_run(void);\n\n")
